# Local development/testing runs against a local Docker Postgres instance
# (docker-compose.yml + LOCAL_DATABASE_SETUP.md) — Supabase is reserved for
# staging/production only (see DEPLOYMENT.md). Three separate connections,
# deliberately different roles/databases (P0-06 / P1 §1 privilege split,
# extended to a fourth for the dedicated test database — see DATABASE.md's
# "Connection Roles" and SECURITY.md §5). Never collapse these back into
# fewer connection strings.

# --- Local development (his_dev) ------------------------------------------

# Runtime connection — used by the running application (src/lib/db.ts) for
# every request. Restricted, non-owner role: full CRUD everywhere except
# UPDATE/DELETE on audit_log/clinical_access_log. `npm run db:local:start` +
# `npm run db:dev:setup` create and grant this automatically for local dev
# (prisma/db-setup/local-init.sql + local-grant-runtime-role.sql).
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://his_app_runtime:his_app_runtime_dev_only@localhost:5433/his_dev?schema=public"

# Migration connection — used only by the Prisma CLI (migrate/generate/db
# seed, see prisma.config.ts). Owner-level DDL rights the runtime role
# intentionally lacks. Never used by the running application at request time.
DIRECT_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5433/his_dev?schema=public"

# --- Integration tests (his_test) ------------------------------------------

# The dedicated test database's runtime/owner connections — same roles/
# privilege split as above, pointed at `his_test` instead of `his_dev`.
# The test bootstrap (test/setup-test-database.ts) substitutes these for
# DATABASE_URL/DIRECT_DATABASE_URL automatically for every test run — the
# integration suite NEVER uses the two vars above. `npm run db:test:setup`
# creates/grants these; `npm run db:test:reset` wipes and rebuilds `his_test`
# from scratch. See LOCAL_DATABASE_SETUP.md.
#
# The integration suite must never point these at Supabase or any other
# hosted/shared database — the test bootstrap refuses to run if either one
# looks like it does (see scripts/db/lib.ts's assertNotRemoteHost).
TEST_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://his_app_runtime:his_app_runtime_dev_only@localhost:5433/his_test?schema=public"
TEST_DIRECT_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5433/his_test?schema=public"

# P4.5 §11/§12: a third, separate local database — never his_dev/his_test,
# never production — dedicated to load testing. `npm run db:load-test:setup`
# creates/migrates/grants it; load-tests/seed/generate-load-data.ts fills it
# with a realistic synthetic dataset. Every load-test script refuses to run
# against anything but a connection string whose database name is literally
# "his_load_test" (assertIsLoadTestDatabase, scripts/db/lib.ts) — there is no
# override. See load-tests/README.md.
LOAD_TEST_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://his_app_runtime:his_app_runtime_dev_only@localhost:5433/his_load_test?schema=public"
LOAD_TEST_DIRECT_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5433/his_load_test?schema=public"

# --- Staging/production (Supabase) -----------------------------------------
#
# A deployed environment (staging/production) sets DATABASE_URL/
# DIRECT_DATABASE_URL to its Supabase project's connection strings instead
# of the local values above — see DEPLOYMENT.md's "Environment Variables"
# and "Deployment Checklist" for the exact format (the runtime connection
# MUST use Supabase's Supavisor pooler in TRANSACTION mode, port 6543,
# `?pgbouncer=true` — never session mode, port 5432; DEPLOYMENT.md explains
# the real outage that caused). TEST_DATABASE_URL/TEST_DIRECT_DATABASE_URL
# are not set at all in a deployed environment — nothing there runs the
# integration suite.

SESSION_SECRET="replace-with-a-long-random-string"
NODE_ENV="development"
STORAGE_DRIVER="local"

# Outbox reliability (P1 §3/§4 — see DEPLOYMENT.md's "Outbox Sweep
# Scheduling"). Both optional; sensible defaults apply if unset.

# Secret Vercel Cron (or any other scheduler) must present as
# `Authorization: Bearer <value>` to call /api/cron/outbox-sweep. Leave unset
# in local development — the route refuses every request rather than running
# unauthenticated, and nothing in local dev needs the periodic sweep anyway
# (dispatchPendingOutboxEvents already fires inline after every write).
# CRON_SECRET="replace-with-a-long-random-string"

# How long (ms) an event may sit in "processing" before it's presumed
# crashed and returned to the retry queue. Default: 300000 (5 minutes) —
# only set this if a real deployment's handlers are legitimately slower than
# that (see src/lib/platform/outbox.ts's own comment for the reasoning).
# OUTBOX_PROCESSING_TIMEOUT_MS="300000"
